    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d562-a3">

                <pb facs="0671" n="575" xml:id="pg575"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Reyes to
                            Bluefields Board of Trade.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bluefields</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-12-10"><hi rendition="#italic">December 10,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: I received your attentive dispatch of
                    to-day’s date.</p>
                <p>You can rest assured that I will do all in my power that the tariff of September
                    1 is not declared in force in this littoral, and that I shall spare no efforts
                    in securing this.</p>
                <p>I highly appreciate the wishes you cherish of seeing me remain here, and it will
                    be a pleasure to me to prove myself worthy of these acts of good government.</p>
                <p>Expressingto you my smcerest consideration, I remain, your attentive servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. P. Reyes.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
